---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Cookies and your choices"
  description="Control essential, analytics, and advertising storage on More Than Mildly."
  ><div class="container legal-page">
    <span class="eyebrow">YOUR PRIVACY</span><h1>Cookies & your choices.</h1><p
      class="legal-date"
    >
      Last updated 6 September 2026
    </p><div class="prose">
      <p>
        We use storage to keep this website working and remember choices you
        make. Optional analytics and advertising technologies stay off unless
        you choose to allow them. You can read articles without accepting
        optional cookies.
      </p><button class="button" data-open-consent
        >Manage cookie preferences</button
      ><h2>What we use</h2><div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead
            ><tr
              ><th>Purpose</th><th>Storage</th><th>When it is used</th><th
                >Duration</th
              ></tr
            ></thead
          ><tbody
            ><tr
              ><td>Your preferences</td><td>mtm_consent, mtm_theme</td><td
                >To remember cookie and theme choices</td
              ><td>Consent: 400 days; theme: until cleared</td></tr
            ><tr
              ><td>Likes and notifications</td><td>mtm_visitor</td><td
                >Only after you request a feature; a signed identifier prevents
                duplicate likes and manages your subscription</td
              ><td>180 days</td></tr
            ><tr
              ><td>Admin authentication</td><td
                >nf_jwt and Identity session storage</td
              ><td>When an administrator signs in</td><td
                >Session duration set by the authentication service</td
              ></tr
            ><tr
              ><td>Analytics</td><td>Google Analytics, including _ga cookies</td
              ><td>Only when configured and you accept analytics</td><td
                >Provider configured; commonly up to two years</td
              ></tr
            ><tr
              ><td>Advertising measurement</td><td
                >Meta and TikTok pixels, including _fbp, _fbc, and _ttp</td
              ><td>Only when enabled, configured, and separately permitted</td
              ><td>Provider configured; review before activation</td></tr
            ><tr
              ><td>Installation</td><td>Service worker cache</td><td
                >To display the app icon and an offline page</td
              ><td>Until the app is removed or site data is cleared</td></tr
            ></tbody>
        </table>
      </div><h2>Rejecting or withdrawing consent</h2><p>
        Use Cookie preferences in the footer to turn optional categories off.
        Withdrawing consent stops future use by this site and removes known
        optional first-party cookies where the browser permits. It does not
        erase data a provider already received; you can request help with that
        through our <a href="/privacy#request">privacy request form</a>.
      </p><h2>Do not sell or share my personal information</h2><p>
        Use the link below to turn off advertising tracking on this browser. We
        also respect the Global Privacy Control signal by keeping advertising
        tracking off. These settings do not require an account.
      </p><a class="button secondary" href="/cookies?optout=1"
        >Do not sell or share my personal information</a
      ><h2>Advertising and younger readers</h2><p>
        Advertising measurement is disabled by default for this publication.
        Displaying a contextual advertisement does not require optional
        tracking. Any future use of advertising pixels must account for the
        audience, applicable consent rules, and the providers’ requirements.
      </p><h2>Browser settings</h2><p>
        You can clear site data or block cookies using your browser settings.
        Clearing data removes your saved choices and may also remove likes
        remembered on this device, notification settings, or an admin session.
      </p><p>
        For more about personal information and your rights, read our <a
          href="/privacy">privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div></Layout
>
